"style": "BodyText", "text": "According to expert opinion, the blood transfusion threshold for patients with colonic bleeding is a haemoglobin value <9 g/dL (note this is different for the evidence-based threshold for UGI bleeding).", "runs": [{"text": "According to expert opinion, the blood transfusion threshold for patients with colonic bleeding is a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "haemoglobin value <9 g/dL (note this is different for the evidence-based threshold for UGI bleeding)."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1504"}}, {"id": "body-09189-textbox1-00003", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "If the patient is hemodynamically unstable, resuscitate the patient before diagnostic studies are performed. Most episodes of LGI bleeding resolve spontaneously.", "runs": [{"text": "If"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patient"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hemodynamically"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "unstable,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "resuscitate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patient"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "before"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "diagnostic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "studies"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "performed. Most episodes of LGI bleeding resolve spontaneously."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1504"}}, {"id": "body-09189-textbox1-00004", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Colonoscopy is recommended early, usually within the first 48 hours of admission, and endoscopic therapy is used to control continued bleeding.", "runs": [{"text": "Colonoscopy is recommended early, usually within the first 48 hours of admission, and endoscopic therapy is used to control continued bleeding."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1504"}}, {"id": "body-09189-textbox1-00005", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "If colonoscopy does not identify a discrete lesion or endoscopic therapy does not cont